                        "sense_id": "9d4a337b-995f-3b0f-b888-53e6eee99d99",
                        "entry_id": "7988034e-c87e-329c-b226-32e3840f8ba6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Capable or deserving of being kicked."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "34479987-8a50-41eb-9bcb-62915ed78813",
                                "sense_id": "9d4a337b-995f-3b0f-b888-53e6eee99d99",
                                "text": "The home side were showing adventure, running from deep in their own half and booting a kickable penalty to touch."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bda84d2b-d463-4630-988b-a157fc2f0cb9",
                                "sense_id": "9d4a337b-995f-3b0f-b888-53e6eee99d99",
                                "text": "I look at her as the very gizzard of a trifle, […] fitter to be kickt, if ſhee vvere of a kickable ſubſtance, than either honoured or humoured."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "76230614-c962-48ce-a7f7-2834ed617862",
                                "sense_id": "9d4a337b-995f-3b0f-b888-53e6eee99d99",
                                "text": "Kickable people are of various descriptions. Amongst these are your kickable subjects prima facie;—those whose provocatives are visible and external, whose incentives to you to kick them lie chiefly in manner and bearing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "efe98b7b-223f-4bc2-af81-9b090dce44d4",
                                "sense_id": "9d4a337b-995f-3b0f-b888-53e6eee99d99",
                                "text": "All sorts of kickable objects were used from ancient times until today's inflated ball, with a leather casing between 27 and 28 inches in circumference, was adopted."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dc9a357e-ee33-4629-bd5f-8e16d53fb70a",
                                "sense_id": "9d4a337b-995f-3b0f-b888-53e6eee99d99",
                                "text": "The weekend inventor has five U.S. patents and three more pending for inspirations such as a kickable Frisbee, a clothes-ironing mitt and a leak-proof shower curtain."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0733f9a2-64c0-30bd-a304-bc583851ce49",
                        "entry_id": "7988034e-c87e-329c-b226-32e3840f8ba6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Incurring kicking."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dcb13ae9-e7ed-48e3-8b28-df6b1d5176cf",
                                "sense_id": "0733f9a2-64c0-30bd-a304-bc583851ce49",
                                "text": "Insolence of office is pre-eminently kickable. Who ever went into a public office, and was treated, as he is very apt to be, with the most offensive hauteur by some saucy, well-paid official, without feeling the desire to kick him rising strong within him? […] Petty tyranny is also eminently kickable."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1592cdd8-94cb-47c9-8226-8d274deecdb6",
                                "sense_id": "0733f9a2-64c0-30bd-a304-bc583851ce49",
                                "text": "The first serious outbreak and renewal of hostilites ^([sic]) occurred when Dolly—who was now out of the doctor's hands—one morning sent his footman off at a moment's notice, for gross impertinence of the severest kickable kind."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bb4bff30-f077-43bd-8256-dd767e1dcfef",
                                "sense_id": "0733f9a2-64c0-30bd-a304-bc583851ce49",
                                "text": "What if the very things you like in me now—you'd hate sometime. What if the things I think are strong and stunning in you now, I'd think were pig-headed and kickable after a while?"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
